<title>SWEDEN: Stora posts sharp fall in 9 mo profits.</title>
<headline>Stora posts sharp fall in 9 mo profits.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry group Stora AB on Thursday reported its results for the nine months to September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		  1,922 vs  6,198</p>
<p> Invoiced sales			   34,250 vs 43,261</p>
<p> Operating costs			  29,311 vs 33,836</p>
<p> EPS (SKR)				    3.95 vs  12.80</p>
<p> Non-recurring items			  41 vs    315</p>
<p> Depreciation				2,658 vs  2,754</p>
<p> Net financial items		CHARGE 400 vs    788 CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					     650 vs  2,045</p>
<p> Minorities					6 vs     45</p>
<p> Net profit				  1,266 vs  4,108</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full company name is Stora AB.</p>
<p>A Reuters poll of analysts found a market consensus of 1.89 billion crowns for the nine month profit after financial items.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
